n, env allowlist, stdout/stderr byte caps) on top — rather than a parallel launcher that re-derives reaper/timeout logic.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.884,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Close stdin, create a process group/session ... terminate then kill and reap the whole group'; 'Apply the existing 60-second deadline'","harness.run_tool already does: start_new_session=True, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, _reap_process_group (SIGTERM->grace->SIGKILL), _resolve_timeout default 60s / REBAR_GROUNDING_TIMEOUT (src/rebar/grounding/harness.py:131-230)","8+ existing run_tool call-sites: resolve.py:204/224/298, engine_b_backends.py:46/59/249/383/486, pyright_backend.py:59/72"],"finding":"The plan specifies a large bespoke hardened-execution surface (canonicalize PATH basename, reject non-regular/repo-contained candidates, no-shell absolute-path invoke, close stdin, create process group/session, env allowlist, terminate/kill/reap the whole group, cap stdout 4 MiB / stderr 64 KiB, apply 'the existing 60-second deadline') without stating whether it wraps the established harness.run_tool boundary or builds a parallel launcher. run_tool already provides process-group reaping (killpg SIGTERM->grace->SIGKILL), the 60-second REBAR_GROUNDING_TIMEOUT deadline, stdin=DEVNULL, start_new_session, env passthrough, and no_tool/timeout/version_skew fail-open mapping used by 8+ existing backends (resolve.py, engine_b_backends.py, pyright_backend.py). Making the reuse explicit avoids re-implementing reaper/timeout/spawn logic that already exists.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa7e0b40d8945625c","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope → Hardened execution (bullets 1–4)","norm_id":"nc02e2655e1fa3322","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer writes a fresh Popen launcher and re-derives reaper/timeout constants, drifting from the shared harness reaper (grace/drain) and the env-